-- Tests for drink-driving.l4: the same rule, asked under two vintages of the law.
--
-- The rule never changes. What changes between the two #EVALs in section 2 is the
-- rule-effective date pinned by `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT`: the day before the
-- Traffic Ordinance Amendment (No. 97) Law was published, and the day it was.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `drink-driving`

-- Section 7's unpinned case reads today's date, which needs a zone; TIMEZONE is per document.
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Jerusalem"

§ `1. The drivers`

-- Neither a new driver nor under 24, in a private car: paragraph (3A) never reaches her.
`a 40-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` MEANS
    Driver WITH `is a new driver` IS FALSE
                `age in years`    IS 40
                `vehicle driven`  IS `private vehicle`

-- Under 24: paragraph (3A)(b). Roznai's reader.
`a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` MEANS
    Driver WITH `is a new driver` IS FALSE
                `age in years`    IS 22
                `vehicle driven`  IS `private vehicle`

-- A new driver, whatever the age: paragraph (3A)(a).
`a 30-year-old new driver, driving a private car` MEANS
    Driver WITH `is a new driver` IS TRUE
                `age in years`    IS 30
                `vehicle driven`  IS `private vehicle`

-- A public vehicle: paragraph (3A)(d).
`a 40-year-old bus driver` MEANS
    Driver WITH `is a new driver` IS FALSE
                `age in years`    IS 40
                `vehicle driven`  IS `public vehicle`

-- A commercial vehicle over 3,500 kg: paragraph (3A)(c).
`a 40-year-old driving a 4,000 kg lorry` MEANS
    Driver WITH `is a new driver` IS FALSE
                `age in years`    IS 40
                `vehicle driven`  IS `commercial or work vehicle` 4000

-- A commercial vehicle of exactly 3,500 kg: "עולה על 3,500" is not met.
`a 40-year-old driving a 3,500 kg van` MEANS
    Driver WITH `is a new driver` IS FALSE
                `age in years`    IS 40
                `vehicle driven`  IS `commercial or work vehicle` 3500

§ `2. One rule, two dates -- the Roznai scenario`

-- A 22-year-old blows 100 micrograms per litre. Under the text of 8 December 2010
-- she is under the general 240; under the text of 9 December 2010 she is over the
-- 50 that paragraph (3A) sets for a driver under 24.
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100))
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100))

#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `intoxicated`

-- The same story on a blood sample: 30 mg per 100 ml is under 50 and over 10.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`blood sample` 30)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`blood sample` 30)) EQUALS `intoxicated`

-- And as the s.62(3) offence: lawful on the 8th, an offence on the 9th.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver commits the offence under section 62(3)` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver commits the offence under section 62(3)` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `3. Amendment 97 does not reach a driver outside paragraph (3A)`

-- The 40-year-old in her own car reads 100 on both days and is under the general
-- threshold on both.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`

-- And over the general threshold on both.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 241)) EQUALS `intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 241)) EQUALS `intoxicated`

§ `4. Every class paragraph (3A) lists flips on 9 December 2010`

#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 30-year-old new driver, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 30-year-old new driver, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `intoxicated`

#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old bus driver` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old bus driver` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `intoxicated`

#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 8) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old driving a 4,000 kg lorry` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old driving a 4,000 kg lorry` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `intoxicated`

-- Exactly 3,500 kg is not "over 3,500": the van driver stays on the general threshold.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old driving a 3,500 kg van` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`

§ `5. "Exceeds" -- the boundaries`

-- Post-Amendment 97, a listed driver at exactly 50 micrograms or exactly 10 milligrams
-- is not above the figure.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 50)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 51)) EQUALS `intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`blood sample` 10)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`blood sample` 11)) EQUALS `intoxicated`

-- The general threshold's own boundaries, for a driver outside paragraph (3A).
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 240)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`blood sample` 50)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 40-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`blood sample` 51)) EQUALS `intoxicated`

§ `6. What the encoding refuses to answer`

-- Before 10 November 2009 the Regulations defined "המידה הקבועה" in words this
-- encoding has not read. It says so instead of extrapolating (NOTES.md, fork F2).
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2009 11 9) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2009 11 9)  (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `the text in force on that date is not encoded`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2009 11 10) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2009 11 9)  (`the driver commits the offence under section 62(3)` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `7. The other axes`

-- No pin at all: the rule-effective date falls back to today, long after 2010.
#ASSERT `the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100) EQUALS `intoxicated`

-- Pin only the FACTS to a day before the amendment. With no rule-version pin, the
-- rule-effective date follows the valid-time axis: the law in force when the driver
-- was stopped applies, which is the presumption against retroactivity.
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (YMD 2010 6 1) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (YMD 2010 6 1) (`the driver is intoxicated` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100)) EQUALS `not intoxicated`

-- Not on a road or in a public place: intoxicated, but not the s.62(3) offence.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2010 12 9) (`the driver commits the offence under section 62(3)` `a 22-year-old with a full licence, driving a private car` (`breath sample` 100) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
